    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #370\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-216-implementation-audit-fixes-10-23-add-d-thr_yg7w6yw8u2` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #216: retained doc-history model for the Yjs CRDT persistence layer.\n\n- **`doc_history_updates`** table mirrors every `doc_updates` append (same id/bytes/attribution/timestamp) in the same transaction, with its own `expires_at`.\n- **`doc_snapshot_history`** gained `through_update_id`, `represented_at`, and a nullable `expires_at`; **`docs`** gained `history_available_from`. New docs atomically get a non-expiring baseline checkpoint (`through_update_id = 0`) at creation.\n- **Compaction** now writes a checkpoint matching the exact contract (boundary = greatest merged update's id/`created_at`, `expires_at` = represented_at + retention) in the same transaction as the snapshot write and `doc_updates` delete, and never touches `doc_history_updates` or the NULL-expiry baseline. The old periodic squash sweep (`squashDocHistory`/`runHistorySquashSweep`/`handleDocHistorySquashTask`) is removed entirely, including its cron entry and task name.\n- **`openDocVersionAt`** rejects future timestamps (`ValidationError`), returns the empty doc before the first update, selects the latest applicable checkpoint and replays `doc_history_updates` forward, and returns `HistoryNotRetainedError` (HTTP 410 `history_not_retained`) before `history_available_from` or before the retention cutoff.\n- **`DOC_HISTORY_RETENTION_DAYS`** config (default 30) validates as a positive integer; retention math uses `make_interval(hours => 24 * days)` against `transaction_timestamp()` for DST/timezone-safe boundaries.\n- **`0035_doc_history_retention.sql`** adds everything additively (nullable), per expand/contract migration discipline; **`docHistoryCutoverMigration.ts`** (JS, since it merges Yjs binary updates) runs once after `runMigrations` to delete every ambiguous pre-#216 checkpoint, install one valid cutover baseline per doc, and only then tighten the new columns to NOT NULL — covered by a populated-migration test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `test:unit` — 23 files / 159 tests passed\n- `test:integration` — 78 files / 904 tests passed\n- `test:e2e` — 1 file / 5 tests passed\n- Workspace-wide `tsc --noEmit` — clean\n- `eslint .` — clean\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
