    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #370\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-216-implementation-audit-fixes-10-23-add-d-thr_yg7w6yw8u2` (`b97602a..7c03b76`).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddresses the code-review feedback on PR #370 (`https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/102901029353`):\n\n**Open medium findings:**\n- `docPersistence.ts` — compaction checkpoint `expires_at` was anchored to the boundary update's `created_at` (content time) rather than compaction time, so a dormant doc's checkpoint could already be expired the moment it was written. Now anchored to `transaction_timestamp()`.\n- `runMigrationsCli.ts` — added an addendum to the expand/contract migrations ADR (`docs/adr/2026-09-10-expand-contract-forward-only-migrations.md`) documenting when/how application-code post-migration steps like `docHistoryCutoverMigration.ts` are warranted, invoked, and guarded.\n\n**Unmet acceptance criteria:**\n1. `DOC_HISTORY_RETENTION_DAYS` is now validated eagerly at service startup (`serve.ts`), failing startup on an invalid value instead of only failing lazily on first doc read/write.\n2. `doc_snapshot_history.through_update_id` now has `DEFAULT 0`, matching the spec.\n3. The retention-cutoff boundary tests in `docs.test.ts` now pin the session timezone to UTC and derive all \"now\" values from a single `transaction_timestamp()` read, eliminating clock-skew nondeterminism between Node and Postgres.\n\nWhile writing the ADR addendum, also closed the TOCTOU race it documents: `docHistoryCutoverMigration.ts`'s idempotency check now runs inside the transaction, after the exclusive lock is held.\n\nVerified with the full check battery before pushing: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint` clean, `prettier --check` clean, `test:unit` 25/25 files (177 tests), `test:integration` 81/81 files (912 tests), `test:e2e` 5/5.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
