    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #370\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-216-implementation-audit-fixes-10-23-add-d-thr_yg7w6yw8u2` (`7c03b76..f48140a`).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddresses the second round of code-review feedback on PR #370 (`https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/102917765071`):\n\n**Unmet acceptance criterion #30:** Reverted the compaction checkpoint's `expires_at` back to `represented_at + make_interval(hours => ...)`, matching the issue's Task exactly. The previous round's deviation (anchoring to `transaction_timestamp()`) was unnecessary — `doc_history_updates` is mirrored and never touched by compaction, so an expired compaction checkpoint just means a query falls back to an earlier, non-expiring baseline and replays a longer stretch of the mirrored log; it never produces incorrect state or an incorrect `history_not_retained`.\n\n**Open medium finding:** The previous round's ADR addendum rewrote the body of an already-`accepted` ADR, violating the repo's ADR convention that a file's body stays a historical record. Reverted that edit and moved the content into its own new ADR, `docs/adr/2026-09-10-app-code-post-migration-steps.md`, cross-referenced from the original's Consequences section.\n\n**Low-priority findings:**\n- Schema-qualified the `doc_snapshot_history` idempotency-guard queries (in both `docHistoryCutoverMigration.ts` and its test) with `table_schema = current_schema()`.\n- The boundary tests' `SET TIME ZONE 'UTC'` was session-scoped and could leak onto a pooled connection reused by a later, unrelated test. Now scoped to a dedicated client that resets the timezone before releasing back to the pool.\n\nVerified with the full check battery before pushing: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint` clean, `prettier --check` clean, `test:unit` 25/25 files (177 tests), `test:integration` 81/81 files (912 tests), `test:e2e` 5/5, migration numbering script clean (36 unique ordinals).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
